Try XSLT, in which a function call that in C might look like:

  int x = foo(bar(y));

becomes:

  <xsl:variable name="x">
     <xsl:call-template name="foo">
        <xsl:with-param name="n">
           <xsl:call-template name="bar">
              <xsl:with-param name="n" select="$y"/>
           </xsl:call-template>
        </xsl:with-param>
     </xsl:call-template>
  </xsl:variable>

which is why I love it. (Not that conventional thinking in terms of procedures
and assignments is good practice in XSLT.)

One good thing about that kind of syntax is it more or less enforces a
consistent indent style.

